{
  "id": "ss.relic.sun-struck",
  "name": "Sun-struck",
  "description": "A sun sitting low over a strip of baked pan, with the crust split under it. The disc is small and the rays are long and uneven, which is how a sun reads when it has been up too long; the pan below is a flat sand band with two dark cracks and nothing growing on it. No horizon line and no sky \u2014 the plate's own light is the sky \u2014 so the object is only the two things the find is about: the sun, and how long you have stood under it.",
